      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm currently working on digitizing a collection of 19th-century hand-drawn maps for our university library. I'm running into some issues with the Dublin Core implementation regarding creator attribution. We have several maps where the cartographer is completely unknown or the signature is illegible. How should we handle these \"unidentified\" or \"ambiguous\" creators in the metadata fields to maintain archival integrity without making false assumptions about the origin?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For undiscoverable or illegible creator information, utilize the placeholder 'unknown' or 'ambiguous' in the creator field of the Dublin Core. Provide context in the descriptions or annotations explaining these conditions to preserve the record's integrity without speculating or inaccurately attributing the work.",
